  atspi-scenario-e2e: 15 assertion(s) failed

rc=2 is clap refusing `reproit __atspi`: the command moved under the `internal`
multiplex in d957df5 and the top-level spelling stopped existing. Neither actor
process ever started, which is why all four surviving PASS lines are of the form
"this bad marker is ABSENT" and every failure is of the form "this marker is
PRESENT". A process that produces no output satisfies the first kind for free.

Both actors, both instances, and the full interleaving after the fix, same
container, same script:

  atspi-scenario-e2e: all assertions passed   (19/19)

The other two harnesses carrying the same dead spelling, also gates:

  validation/backends/run-tui.sh:15          -> gate tui-pty
  examples/qt-fixture/qt-atspi-e2e.sh:144,161,171 -> gate linux-atspi-toolkits

Both pass after the fix: "Tui backend passed native curses PTY runtime" and
"wxWidgets AT-SPI runtime passed".

